+## Request measurement and public API contract
+
+`PocketRuntime.measure_request(request)` accepts the same caller-shaped `SynthesisRequest` as strict synthesis, applies the same request/text/language/unsupported-feature validation, and encodes the complete text once. It returns `RequestMeasure(amount, maximum, unit="tokens", fits=...)`; an oversized request has `fits=False` without raising a capacity exception. Synthesis consumes the same private encoded-request helper and raises `SynthesisInputTooLongError` before inference when that measurement does not fit. Measurement does not prepare voices, download assets, perform inference, or call either model or sentence splitters.
+
+The root package exports `RequestMeasure`, `REQUEST_API_VERSION`, `RequestApiContract`, and `request_api_contract()`. Contract version 1 declares the request/result/runtime types and public method names, caller-owned text boundaries, and explicit capability flags. Building the descriptor does not inspect files or caches, install a bundle, open a runtime, or prepare a voice. Pocket supports named, reference, and managed reference voices and voice-level configuration; it does not support linguistic tokens, pronunciation overrides, whole-request phonemes, or word timings. Typed public asset/catalog/session/runtime errors are also exported from the package root.
+
 ## Runtime and bundle lifecycle

 `PocketRuntime.load(directory)` opens a concrete local bundle without network access. `PocketRuntime.from_pretrained(bundle)` resolves and opens a managed bundle through OnnxVoice. Both expose bundle metadata, language, sample rate, predefined voices, voice preparation, token inference, diagnostics, and idempotent close/context-manager lifecycle.
